src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol:unstakeAndExitPool|class=C23|Medium|The post-exit re-wrap is gated on the two hardcoded conditions ASSET == address(WETH) and TOKEN_x == ETH_ADDRESS, so a V1/StableSwapNG pool with a real native-ETH leg but a non-WETH asset (pool [ETH, USDC], asset = USDC) leaves raw ETH in the vault, and __initiateWithdraw then calls manager.initiateWithdraw for that leg with a non-zero yieldTokenAmount but no msg.value and no approval (the ETH sentinel short-circuits checkApprove), recording a withdraw request backed by tokens the manager never received — a phantom escrow that the convertToAssets escrow branch will happily value.|src/single-sided-lp/CurveConvex2Token.sol
